      "direction": "monolith_slab",
      "name": "Monolith Slab Detector",
      "form_language": "A single, calm slab with a soft chamfered perimeter that reads as one continuous surface from any angle. The chamfer is generous enough to remove visual weight while keeping the front face flat and glare-resistant. A subtle recessed intake grille on the top face separates the display zone from the sensing zone without breaking the monolithic read. The overall gesture is quiet, confident, and friendly through proportion rather than ornament.",
