      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the front display window at least 54 x 24 mm with a 1.5 m readability target; do not shrink below 50 x 22 mm without re-verifying readability from a neighbouring desk.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Preserve the single chamfered-slab silhouette with a continuous 10 mm corner radius and no secondary part lines on the front face; any split lines must be moved to the back or bottom.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Use textured_light finish on all visible A-surface housing walls to hide fingerprints and reduce glare; do not polish the front bezel.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Specify rABS as the primary housing material with a minimum 30% recycled content, subject to drop-test and colour-match approval; fall back to ABS only if rABS fails durability or cost targets.",
          "category": "sustainability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Keep the top-face intake recessed and offset from the display centreline so it does not read as a second screen; maintain a minimum 8 mm clearance from the front chamfer.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA6",
          "statement": "Hold the housing BOM at or below CNY 18/unit at 10,000 units/year; the 2-shot pad-print graphic is the only decorative secondary op allowed.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "This variant adapts the tooling-approved reference by keeping the proven rounded-rectangle DNA but stretching the plan to 122 x 72 mm and reducing height to 26 mm for a slimmer, more modern slab. The corner radius is raised from 8 mm to 10 mm to soften the chamfered silhouette and reinforce the friendly, approachable brief. The 54 x 24 mm display window is the largest that fits the front face with adequate bezel and is sized for readability from roughly 1.5 m, directly answering Q1's default assumption. The top intake is a shallow recessed grille that separates sensing from display while preserving the monolith read and avoids front-face perforation, which would collect dust and fingerprints. USB-C is placed on the back for clean cable management in open-plan desks. Material is rABS with textured_light finish, meeting the sustainability priority at 0.3 and the fingerprint-hiding must-have; rABS is cost-neutral against ABS at volume and keeps the BOM inside the CNY 18 ceiling. The single pad-print op adds brand and status legibility without tooling cost. All choices stay within the 125 x 75 x 30 mm envelope and leave margin for a 92 g internal stack under the 180 g mass limit."
    },
